#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:171
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:173
msgid "If webhooks aren't working:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:175
msgid ""
"**Is the gateway running?** Check with `systemctl --user status hermes-"
"gateway` or `ps aux | grep gateway`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:176
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Is the webhook server listening?** `curl http://localhost:8644/health` "
"should return `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:177
msgid ""
"**Check gateway logs:** `grep webhook ~/.hermes/logs/gateway.log | tail "
"-20`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:178
msgid ""
"**Signature mismatch?** Verify the secret in your service matches the one"
" from `hermes webhook list`. GitHub sends `X-Hub-Signature-256`, GitLab "
"sends `X-Gitlab-Token`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:179
msgid ""
"**Firewall/NAT?** The webhook URL must be reachable from the service. For"
" local development, use a tunnel (ngrok, cloudflared)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/webhook-subscriptions_SKILL.md:180
msgid ""
"**Wrong event type?** Check `--events` filter matches what the service "
"sends. Use `hermes webhook test <name>` to verify the route works."
msgstr ""

